Z||000000||Gold-86SE||10-17-2000||12:43 PM||||<BR>since, my last went unanswered let me post this again, under a different title.<P>I did a search, but did not find answers to my questions, so here they are.<P>I am going to be mating an 85 Iron Duke to an 84 4.10 4 speed tranny.<P>I was looking at the FS to see what they had and prices for it. Now, here is my question - will the 85-86 4 SPEED HEAVY DUTY CLUTCH KIT" work in this application? I ask because V6 is not specified, here is the link: <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo_pegasus.asp?number=54002&variation=&aitem=10&mitem=18" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secureleadercom.com/store/prodinfo_pegasus.asp?number=54002&variation=&aitem=10&mitem=18</A>  <P>Second, providing that this works, will a HD clutch be heavy and require a lot of left foot work?<P>Third, how long of a life will a HD clutch give me in this application?<P>The FS shows a clutch, pressure plate, throwout bearing, and alignment tool for just under what they are asking for the 85-86 HD clutch. But, if the 85-86 HD clutch will work, I am leaning that direction.<P>I want a clutch that will last me, at minimum, 80k miles. The 84 is not my performance machine, just my runabout.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.txconnect.com/home/rharris/signature-a.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-17-2000||02:39 PM||||Well, apparently no one knows for sure.  But I'll offer an opinion...<P>My guess is that the clutch package would be compatible with <B>both</B> the V6 and Iron Duke interfaces.<BR>  <BR>Reasons: 1) FS blerb doesn't specify which engine their package goes with, as you point out, so I assume it's good for both.  2) Back when I was looking for a replacement clutch, local parts stores claimed that the packages were the same for both engines.<P>As far as left leg work goes, the FS blerb claims, "will not increase clutch pedal pressure."  <P>Longevity?  My clutch replacement has lasted <B>well</B> over 80,000 miles.  That's with the V6, and wasn't a "heavy duty" clutch (who <B>knows</B> what that really means?).  If FS's package was sized for the V6, and is at least as good as NAPA's (where I got mine, if I recall correctly), I would guess yours will last quite a while.<P>Wish I could offer you some <B>real</B> data, but that's all I know.  Maybe you should write or call FS with your questions.      ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||10-17-2000||03:38 PM||||<BR>Thanks Stu, I'll take the advice and dig further.<BR>||||reg||1
